I'll wire it: in the PATCH handler, when 'vagas' in corpo, compute ocupadas via a query guarded by table existence. Actually, should I wire it now? The R20 test is a unit test only. The skill says minimal code for the test to pass — the unit test passes with just contagem.js. But R20's implementation in the route is part of the rule. Hmm. The spec says "em M1 o teste de unidade cobre o cálculo" — so the acceptance for M1 is the unit test. The route uses it when M2 exists.

But leaving the route without any wiring means R20's guard is dead code in M1. Is that acceptable? Per spec section 7: "os cenários que dependem de inscrições (R20) rodam só quando M2 surgir — até lá o cálculo é provado por teste direto da função de contagem." So yes — in M1 the only proof required is the unit test. But I should still wire the route so that when M2 lands, it works. Let me add the route wiring now as part of R20 implementation. It returns 0 in M1 because there's no inscricoes table.

